architecture: Biashara Bank mobile banking API
  6 components, 6 data flows

shared responsibility model
  Data classification & accountability   customer · customer · customer
  Identity & access management           customer · customer · shared  
  Application security                   customer · customer · provider
  Network controls (firewall rules)      customer · shared   · provider
  Operating system patching              customer · provider · provider
  Hypervisor & host infrastructure       provider · provider · provider
  Physical data centre security          provider · provider · provider

component split
  Mobile app (user)          external customer 0 · shared 0 · provider 0  -> external actor
  API server                 iaas  customer 5 · shared 0 · provider 2  -> customer
  Accounts database          paas  customer 3 · shared 1 · provider 3  -> customer + provider
  Statement files            paas  customer 3 · shared 1 · provider 3  -> customer + provider
  Customer email             saas  customer 1 · shared 1 · provider 5  -> provider
  Statement generator        paas  customer 3 · shared 1 · provider 3  -> customer + provider

flow F1 login: 1 threats
  Spoofing                 CSA #1  owner: customer (the bank's team)
flow F2 balance: 1 threats
  Elevation of privilege   CSA #1  owner: customer (the bank's team)
flow F3 query: 4 threats
  Repudiation              CSA #3  owner: customer (the bank's team)
  Denial of service        CSA #2  owner: shared — provider supplies it, customer must configure it
  Elevation of privilege   CSA #1  owner: customer (the bank's team)
  Information disclosure   CSA #8  owner: customer (the bank's team)
flow F4 statements: 3 threats
  Denial of service        CSA #2  owner: shared — provider supplies it, customer must configure it
  Information disclosure   CSA #11  owner: customer (the bank's team)
  Information disclosure   CSA #8  owner: customer (the bank's team)
flow F5 notify: 2 threats
  Denial of service        CSA #2  owner: provider
  Spoofing                 CSA #6  owner: customer (the bank's team)
flow F6 admin: 1 threats
  Spoofing                 CSA #1  owner: customer (the bank's team)

who owns the work
   9 threats  customer (the bank's team)
   2 threats  shared — provider supplies it, customer must configure it
   1 threat   provider

lock-in
  Mobile app (user)          0/12 (n/a)
  API server                 0/12 (low)
  Accounts database          12/12 (high)
      data      export to an open format (CSV, JSON, SQLite) and prove a restore
      api       keep the call graph in Terraform and put a container or adapter in front
      contract  exit clause naming data-return format, timeline, assistance and a price cap
      skills    cross-train on a second provider; keep runbooks vendor-neutral
  Statement files            3/12 (low)
      api       keep the call graph in Terraform and put a container or adapter in front
  Customer email             0/12 (low)
  Statement generator        12/12 (high)
      data      export to an open format (CSV, JSON, SQLite) and prove a restore
      api       keep the call graph in Terraform and put a container or adapter in front
      contract  exit clause naming data-return format, timeline, assistance and a price cap
      skills    cross-train on a second provider; keep runbooks vendor-neutral

12 threats mapped across 6 CSA categories
